{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EEdEY9iwRMpZuMUJ6tgHVZ","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t\n151\t/* ============================================================\n152\t   CSS Native Scroll-Driven Carousel (US-187)\n153\t   Chrome 135+ proposed ::scroll-button() and ::scroll-marker\n154\t   pseudo-elements for automatic ARIA button roles and\n155\t   keyboard handling. Wrapped in @supports guard for future.\n156\t   Current fallback: scroll-snap CSS with hidden scrollbar.\n157\t   Ensures CLS=0 via fixed aspect-ratio on carousel items.\n158\t   Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/blog/carousels-with-css\n159\t   Spec: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-5/#scroll-marker-group\n160\t   ============================================================ */\n161\t\n162\t/* Future Chrome 135+ native scroll-driven carousel support */\n163\t@supports (selector(::scroll-button(*))) {\n164\t  .carousel-scroll-container {\n165\t    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;\n166\t    scroll-behavior: smooth;\n167\t    overflow-x: auto;\n168\t    scrollbar-width: none;\n169\t    -ms-overflow-style: none;\n170\t  }\n171\t\n172\t  .carousel-scroll-container::-webkit-scrollbar {\n173\t    display: none;\n174\t  }\n175\t\n176\t  .carousel-scroll-container > * {\n177\t    scroll-snap-align: start;\n178\t    scroll-snap-stop: always;\n179\t    flex-shrink: 0;\n180\t  }\n181\t\n182\t  /* Automatic scroll prev/next buttons with built-in ARIA roles */\n183\t  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-button(prev) {\n184\t    @apply w-11 h-11 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-stone-800 shadow-md\n185\t           flex items-center justify-center\n186\t           hover:bg-stone-50 dark:hover:bg-stone-700\n187\t           transition-colors cursor-pointer;\n188\t    position: absolute;\n189\t    left: 0;\n190\t    top: 50%;\n191\t    transform: translateY(-50%);\n192\t    z-index: 20;\n193\t  }\n194\t\n195\t  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-button(next) {\n196\t    @apply w-11 h-11 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-stone-800 shadow-md\n197\t           flex items-center justify-center\n198\t           hover:bg-stone-50 dark:hover:bg-stone-700\n199\t           transition-colors cursor-pointer;\n200\t    position: absolute;\n201\t    right: 0;\n202\t    top: 50%;\n203\t    transform: translateY(-50%);\n204\t    z-index: 20;\n205\t  }\n206\t\n207\t  /* Automatic scroll marker group for keyboard-accessible navigation dots */\n208\t  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-marker {\n209\t    display: flex;\n210\t    gap: 0.5rem;\n211\t    justify-content: center;\n212\t    margin-top: 1rem;\n213\t    flex-wrap: wrap;\n214\t  }\n215\t\n216\t  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-marker-item {\n217\t    @apply w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-stone-300 dark:bg-stone-600\n218\t           cursor-pointer transition-colors;\n219\t  }\n220\t\n221\t  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-marker-item[aria-current=\"true\"] {\n222\t    @apply bg-amber-600 dark:bg-amber-400;\n223\t  }\n224\t}\n225\t\n226\t/* Fallback: browsers without ::scroll-button() support degrade gracefully */\n227\t@supports not (selector(::scroll-button(*))) {\n228\t  .carousel-scroll-container {\n229\t    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;\n230\t    overflow-x: auto;\n231\t    scrollbar-width: none;\n232\t    -ms-overflow-style: none;\n233\t    scroll-behavior: smooth;\n234\t  }\n235\t\n236\t  .carousel-scroll-container::-webkit-scrollbar {\n237\t    display: none;\n238\t  }\n239\t\n240\t  .carousel-scroll-container > * {\n241\t    scroll-snap-align: start;\n242\t    scroll-snap-stop: always;\n243\t    flex-shrink: 0;\n244\t  }\n245\t}\n246\t\n247\t@utility container-custom {\n248\t  /* Container */\n249\t  @apply max-w-6xl mx-auto;\n250\t}\n251\t\n252\t@utility section-label {\n253\t  /* Section label - Elegant uppercase */\n254\t  @apply text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-amber-700 mb-4 dark:text-amber-400;\n255\t}\n256\t\n257\t@utility section-heading {\n258\t  /* Section heading - Serif display font (uses theme --font-display for next/font metric-adjusted fallback) */\n259\t  @apply text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-medium text-stone-900\n260\t           leading-tight tracking-tight dark:text-stone-100;\n261\t  font-family: var(--font-display);\n262\t}\n263\t\n264\t@utility body-text {\n265\t  /* Body text */\n266\t  @apply text-stone-600 leading-relaxed dark:text-stone-400;\n267\t}\n268\t\n269\t@utility card {\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8cb50fe-9df1-48cd-b7a1-251e7a41c10c","uuid":"9c512ce3-03ac-4770-9c6f-3147e2c7a009","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:18:42.569Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\app\\globals.css","content":"\n/* ============================================================\n   CSS Native Scroll-Driven Carousel (US-187)\n   Chrome 135+ proposed ::scroll-button() and ::scroll-marker\n   pseudo-elements for automatic ARIA button roles and\n   keyboard handling. Wrapped in @supports guard for future.\n   Current fallback: scroll-snap CSS with hidden scrollbar.\n   Ensures CLS=0 via fixed aspect-ratio on carousel items.\n   Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/blog/carousels-with-css\n   Spec: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-5/#scroll-marker-group\n   ============================================================ */\n\n/* Future Chrome 135+ native scroll-driven carousel support */\n@supports (selector(::scroll-button(*))) {\n  .carousel-scroll-container {\n    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;\n    scroll-behavior: smooth;\n    overflow-x: auto;\n    scrollbar-width: none;\n    -ms-overflow-style: none;\n  }\n\n  .carousel-scroll-container::-webkit-scrollbar {\n    display: none;\n  }\n\n  .carousel-scroll-container > * {\n    scroll-snap-align: start;\n    scroll-snap-stop: always;\n    flex-shrink: 0;\n  }\n\n  /* Automatic scroll prev/next buttons with built-in ARIA roles */\n  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-button(prev) {\n    @apply w-11 h-11 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-stone-800 shadow-md\n           flex items-center justify-center\n           hover:bg-stone-50 dark:hover:bg-stone-700\n           transition-colors cursor-pointer;\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    top: 50%;\n    transform: translateY(-50%);\n    z-index: 20;\n  }\n\n  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-button(next) {\n    @apply w-11 h-11 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-stone-800 shadow-md\n           flex items-center justify-center\n           hover:bg-stone-50 dark:hover:bg-stone-700\n           transition-colors cursor-pointer;\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 0;\n    top: 50%;\n    transform: translateY(-50%);\n    z-index: 20;\n  }\n\n  /* Automatic scroll marker group for keyboard-accessible navigation dots */\n  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-marker {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 0.5rem;\n    justify-content: center;\n    margin-top: 1rem;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n  }\n\n  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-marker-item {\n    @apply w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-stone-300 dark:bg-stone-600\n           cursor-pointer transition-colors;\n  }\n\n  .carousel-scroll-container::scroll-marker-item[aria-current=\"true\"] {\n    @apply bg-amber-600 dark:bg-amber-400;\n  }\n}\n\n/* Fallback: browsers without ::scroll-button() support degrade gracefully */\n@supports not (selector(::scroll-button(*))) {\n  .carousel-scroll-container {\n    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;\n    overflow-x: auto;\n    scrollbar-width: none;\n    -ms-overflow-style: none;\n    scroll-behavior: smooth;\n  }\n\n  .carousel-scroll-container::-webkit-scrollbar {\n    display: none;\n  }\n\n  .carousel-scroll-container > * {\n    scroll-snap-align: start;\n    scroll-snap-stop: always;\n    flex-shrink: 0;\n  }\n}\n\n@utility container-custom {\n  /* Container */\n  @apply max-w-6xl mx-auto;\n}\n\n@utility section-label {\n  /* Section label - Elegant uppercase */\n  @apply text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-amber-700 mb-4 dark:text-amber-400;\n}\n\n@utility section-heading {\n  /* Section heading - Serif display font (uses theme --font-display for next/font metric-adjusted fallback) */\n  @apply text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-medium text-stone-900\n           leading-tight tracking-tight dark:text-stone-100;\n  font-family: var(--font-display);\n}\n\n@utility body-text {\n  /* Body text */\n  @apply text-stone-600 leading-relaxed dark:text-stone-400;\n}\n\n@utility card {","numLines":120,"startLine":150,"totalLines":886}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01K4smWbyWeYrTFqMaLBc5aK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The CSS looks syntactically correct. The issue might be with how Tailwind is handling the @apply directive in the @supports blocks, or it might be a broader Turbopack issue. Let me check if the issue is related to the @apply directives inside @supports blocks. Tailwind might not handle @apply inside @supports properly.\n\nLet me refactor to avoid using @apply inside @supports blocks, and instead use regular CSS classes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1678,"cache_read_input_tokens":105946,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1678},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8cb50fe-9df1-48cd-b7a1-251e7a41c10c","uuid":"4f16665e-b574-4860-95c5-60205508dcc8"}
